MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
Input is read from whichever stream S10 names. Switching away from one
does not forget where it had reached, and the end of a stream that is
not the revert stream sends input back to the revert stream, which is
this one.
MCDEF GREET AS <a macro defined in the first stream>
MCSET S10=2
The line above ran on the way back, without being asked for. The
environment belongs to the process and not to the stream, so the count
the other one kept is readable here: %P1.
A stream already read to the end has nothing left to give, so asking
for it again comes straight back.
MCSET S10=2
Adding a hundred to the number rewinds the stream first, which is how
a set of macros is given the second pass it needs.
MCSET S10=102
%P1. passes, and this stream carries on from where it was.
